   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Complex/RiemannSurface/Divisor/PointTwist.lean",
   "fix": "Replace the trailing `rfl` with an explicit step, for example `congr 1` followed by `funext z; simp [div_eq_inv_mul]`. Alternatively, state the coordinate-inverse-times-germ identity as a small lemma about `meromorphicGerms.mk` and use it here. At minimum, add a comment saying which definitional unfolding the `rfl` uses.",
   "issue": "`hgerm` rewrites through eight named lemmas (`Subring.coe_mul`, `coe_inv`, `coe_coordinate`, `coe_toChartGerm`, `coe_mk`, `\u2190 Germ.coe_inv`, `\u2190 Germ.coe_mul`, `inv_mul_eq_div`) and then closes with a bare `rfl`. That `rfl` silently relies on the germ of `g / (z - c)` unfolding to the germ of `fun z \u21a6 g z / (z - c)` through `Pi.div` and the `Germ` coercion. The chain is brittle and the reason the final step holds is not stated.",
   "line": 140
  }
